calibration due date will be recorded within subsequent sections of this procedure.\n',7,5,'RUN'),(53,'Operational Constraints','SPP system environmental, EMC/EMI, and safety operational constraints during all phases of the integration of the propulsion system shall be adhered to by all personnel who are either directly or indirectly involved within this procedure.  The specific requirements and guidelines for these constraints are contained in the following documents: SPP Electromagnetic Environment Control Plan (7434-9040), SPP Contamination Control Plan (7434-9011) and SPP System Safety Program Plan (7434-9013).  In addition, specific operational constraints for the propulsion system are contained within the following sections.\n\nTest personnel will be trained and certified in appropriate ESD, cleanroom, security and safety procedures, as applicable.  Only personnel that have received appropriate training and who hold necessary certifications will be allowed to perform activities involving the spacecraft and its components.  \n',8,5,'RUN'),(54,'Propulsion System Contamination Constraints','To avoid contamination of the system, the upstream valve must always be opened prior to the downstream valve.',9,5,'RUN'),(55,'Propulsion System Safety and Handling Constraints','There are no safety constraints concerning the operations in this procedure, and this procedure is not a hazardous operation.\n\nThere are several handling constraints for the propulsion system in this procedure.  When actually firing thrusters, the upstream valve must always be opened prior to the downstream valve.  Thruster covers must also be removed prior to actually firing thrusters.\n',10,5,'RUN'),(56,'Propulsion System Limited Life Items','TBD',11,5,'RUN'),(57,'Scope','This document applies to the electrical integration of the propulsion system to the SPP spacecraft.  This procedure contains supplementary documentation, test equipment, and detailed procedural steps needed for initial integratio