following component integration must have been completed:\n\n•	Ground System Umbilical Interfaces\n•	Power Distribution Unit (PDU)\n•	Redundant Electronics Module (REM)\n•	Redundant Processor Module (RPM) ',5,7,'RUN'),(62,'Ground Support Equipment Configuration','The propulsion system electrical integration requires the spacecraft umbilical GSE (UGSE) and testbed to be connected with the spacecraft.  No propulsion system GSE is required for this procedure.  The diagram below shows the overall test configuration for the propulsion system electrical integration:\n(Figure goes here)',6,7,'RUN'),(63,'Test and Measurement Equipment','Equipment used to perform quantitative measurements shall be Class 1 in accordance with JHU/APL Quality Management System (QMS) document [Q53-055] – JHU/APL Test and Measurement Equipment Practices and Procedures.  \n\nEquipment descriptions along with model, property number and calibration due date will be recorded within subsequent sections of this procedure.\n',7,7,'RUN'),(64,'Operational Constraints','SPP system environmental, EMC/EMI, and safety operational constraints during all phases of the integration of the propulsion system shall be adhered to by all personnel who are either directly or indirectly involved within this procedure.  The specific requirements and guidelines for these constraints are contained in the following documents: SPP Electromagnetic Environment Control Plan (7434-9040), SPP Contamination Control Plan (7434-9011) and SPP System Safety Program Plan (7434-9013).  In addition, specific operational constraints for the propulsion system are contained within the following sections.\n\nTest personnel will be trained and certified in appropriate ESD, cleanroom, security and safety procedures, as applicable.  Only personnel that have received appropriate training and who hold necessary certifications will be allowed to perform activities involving the spacecraft and its components.  \n',8,7,'RUN'),(65,'Propulsion System 