\0'),(2179,'Verify that each propulsion system connector is properly marked per the ICD.   Note the current configuration of each connector (i.e. connector saver installed, EMI cover installed, enable/disable plug installed, flight harness mated, etc. ',2,419,'Step 2',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(2180,'Verify propulsion system harnessing is labeled clearly and is consistent with ICD and Aerojet drawings. ',3,419,'Step 3',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(2181,'Take photographs at this time.  Photos should include views of connectors, labels and assembly part numbers at a minimum.  Place photos in following file location on the SES Davis Drive: ',4,419,'Step 4',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','SINGLE_VALUE','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(2182,'Use micro-ohmmeter to measure resistance from each connector shell to chassis ground for each propulsion system component connector.  Record measurement and verify against expected measurement in the table below.',1,420,'Step 1',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(2183,'Using a Micro Ohmmeter, verify less than 10 milliohms electrical resistance between each component and spacecraft deck.  Note: measurement should be made close to the ground strap point(s).  Record the following information in Step 2.1.',2,420,'Step 2.1',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(2184,' ',3,420,'Step 2.2',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(2185,'The following test equipment will be needed for integration of the propulsion components.  \n	 \nDigital Multi-Meter \nLow Voltage Digital Multi-Meter\nOscilloscope w/ probes\nBOBs and BOB Adapter Cables\nESD Drain Box(s) \n',1,422,'Note:',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(2186,'Verify umbilical connectors are mated.',1,423,'Step 1',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(2187,'Verify the following arm plugs are installed to the spacecraft test panel: Prop Arm A (P0001), Prop Arm B (P0002), and Prop Test (P0003).',2,423,'Step 2',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(2188,'Prior to connecting BOBs to propulsion system or S/C harness connectors, any residual charge must be removed using an ESD Drain.\n\nSteps for installing BOB and Adapter Cables\n1.	Connect harness side and component side adapter cables to BOB\n2.	Connect ESD Drain Box on S/C harness for ~10 seconds \n3.	Remove ESD Drain Box from harness and connect to adapter cable going to S/C harness\n4.	Close all switches on the BOB and connect BOB assembly to< component> connector\n5.	After ~10 seconds open BOB switches and remove ESD Drain Box\n6.	Connect BOB assembly to S/C harness\nPrior to beginning any DMM measurements, simultaneously short test leads together and to S/C ground to remove any residual charge.\nRecord DMM info below:\n',1,424,'Note:',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(2189,'Connect BOB assembly to LV A J1 and to S/C Harness P1601 using the steps outlined in 5.3.  Record BOB and Adapter Cable S/N#.',1,425,'Step 1',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(2190,'Verify all switches on the BOB are set to the “open” position.',2,425,'Step 2',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(2191,'Using a Digital Multi Meter (DMM) configured to measure resistance, perform the following checks and record values looking into LV A J1.  \n\n\nshort test leads together and to S/C ground to remove any residual charge.\n',3,425,'Step 3',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','RUN',NULL,NULL,_bi