nd switching frequency for pressure transducers.',1,663,'Step 1',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3415,'Verify EMC Engineer has completed a magnetic sniff of pressure transducers and latch valves.',2,663,'Step 2',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3416,'Verify measurements fell within expected ranges - or note any deviations or problems below.  Record electronic media file names and location below from EMC testing.',3,663,'Step 3',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3417,'Power down spacecraft.',4,663,'Step 4',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3418,' Enter notes in the table provided as needed.',5,663,'EMC Testing Notes/Deviations/File Names',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3419,'This section contains safe to mates and power/signal checks to be performed to verify the interfaces between the propulsion system thruster valves and catbed heaters and the spacecraft bus.  This section will conclude with the flight mates of the spacecraft harness to the propulsion harness and a full electrical verification of their operation.',1,664,'Note',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3420,'The following test equipment will be needed for integration of the propulsion components.  \n	 \n•	Digital Multi-Meter \n•	Low Voltage Digital Multi-Meter\n•	Oscilloscope w/ probes\n•	BOBs and BOB Adapter Cables\n•	ESD Drain Box(s) \n',1,665,'Note:',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3421,'Verify umbilical connectors are mated.',1,666,'Step 1',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3422,'Verify the following arm plugs are installed to the spacecraft bulkhead panels: Thruster Arm +Y (P1906), Thruster Arm –Y (P4906), Catbed Heater Pri Arm (P4916), and Catbed Heater Red Arm (P4917).',2,666,'Step 2',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3423,'(Attached figure goes here)',3,666,'Figure 6-1: Test Set-up for Section 6',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3424,'Prior to connecting BOBs to propulsion system or S/C harness connectors, any residual charge must be removed using an ESD Drain.\n\nSteps for installing BOB and Adapter Cables\n13.	Connect harness side and component side adapter cables to BOB\n14.	Connect ESD Drain Box on S/C harness for ~10 seconds \n15.	Remove ESD Drain Box from harness and connect to adapter cable going to S/C harness\n16.	Close all switches on the BOB and connect BOB assembly to< component> connector\n17.	After ~10 seconds open BOB switches and remove ESD Drain Box\n18.	Connect BOB assembly to S/C harness\nPrior to beginning any DMM measurements, simultaneously short test leads together and to S/C ground to remove any residual charge.\nRecord DMM info below:',1,667,'Step 1',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3425,'Connect BOB assembly to Propulsion Harness P1905 and to S/C Harness J1905 using the steps outlined in 5.3.  Record BOB and Adapter Cable S/N#.',1,668,'Step 1',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3426,'Verify all switches on the BOB are set to the “open” position.',2,668,'Step 2',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3427,'Using a Digital Multi Meter (DMM) configured to measure resistance, perform the following checks and record values looking into Propulsion Harness P1905.  \n\n\nshort test leads together and to S/C ground to remove any residual charge.\n',3,668,'Step 3',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_b