 the SES Davis Drive: ',1,725,'Step 1',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','SINGLE_VALUE','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3727,'Verify that each propulsion system connector is properly marked per the ICD.   Note the current configuration of each connector (i.e. connector saver installed, EMI cover installed, enable/disable plug installed, flight harness mated, etc. ',2,725,'Step 2',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3728,'Verify propulsion system harnessing is labeled clearly and is consistent with ICD and Aerojet drawings. ',3,725,'Step 3',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3729,'Take photographs at this time.  Photos should include views of connectors, labels and assembly part numbers at a minimum.  Place photos in following file location on the SES Davis Drive: ',4,725,'Step 4',_binary '',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','SINGLE_VALUE','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3730,'Use micro-ohmmeter to measure resistance from each connector shell to chassis ground for each propulsion system component connector.  Record measurement and verify against expected measurement in the table below.',1,726,'Step 1',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3731,'Using a Micro Ohmmeter, verify less than 10 milliohms electrical resistance between each component and spacecraft deck.  Note: measurement should be made close to the ground strap point(s).  Record the following information in Step 2.1.',2,726,'Step 2.1',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3732,' ',3,726,'Step 2.2',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','RUN',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(3733,'The following test equipment will be needed for integration of the propulsion components.  \n	 \nDigital Multi-Meter \nLow Voltage Digital Multi-Meter\nOscilloscope w/ probes\nBOBs an