QA inspector.  Blanks and Tables will indicate where data is required to be filled and/or a verification check is required.  Blanks with role (i.e. Q.A) indicate initials are required.\n************************************************************************************\n',1,1460,'Note:',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','ORIGINAL',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(7131,'Inspect propulsion system for the following items:\n\n•	No nicks, dents or chipped paint\n•	Box and connector cleanliness \n•	Damaged connector pins\n•	Any Missing cable ties \n•	Box screws and connector jackposts are staked\n•	No split washers are used\n\nNote discrepancies/anomalies below and enter Anomaly Report in the SPP Anomaly Problem/Failure Reporting System (APFR) for any non-compliance.  Note any items from incoming Q.A. inspections if any.\n\n\n',1,1461,'Step 1',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','SINGLE_VALUE','ORIGINAL',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(7132,'Verify that each propulsion system connector is properly marked per the ICD.   Note the current configuration of each connector (i.e. connector saver installed, EMI cover installed, enable/disable plug installed, flight harness mated, etc. ',2,1461,'Step 2',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','ORIGINAL',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(7133,'Verify propulsion system harnessing is labeled clearly and is consistent with ICD and Aerojet drawings. ',3,1461,'Step 3',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','ORIGINAL',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(7134,'Take photographs at this time.  Photos should include views of connectors, labels and assembly part numbers at a minimum.  Place photos in following file location on the SES Davis Drive:\n',4,1461,'Step 4',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','SINGLE_VALUE','ORIGINAL',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(7135,'Use micro-ohmmeter to measure resistance from each connector shell to chassis ground for each propulsion system compo