ing an ESD Drain.\n\nSteps for installing BOB and Adapter Cables\n13.	Connect harness side and component side adapter cables to BOB\n14.	Connect ESD Drain Box on S/C harness for ~10 seconds \n15.	Remove ESD Drain Box from harness and connect to adapter cable going to S/C harness\n16.	Close all switches on the BOB and connect BOB assembly to< component> connector\n17.	After ~10 seconds open BOB switches and remove ESD Drain Box\n18.	Connect BOB assembly to S/C harness\nPrior to beginning any DMM measurements, simultaneously short test leads together and to S/C ground to remove any residual charge.\nRecord DMM info below:',1,1545,'Step 1',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','ORIGINAL',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(7509,'Continue L-3 procedure “SPP_propulsion_integration.jpp,” which will initiate the S/C power up procedure.  Record Main Bus Voltage and Current.',1,1547,'Step 1',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','ORIGINAL',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(7510,'Continue script to simulate separation, arm PDU thruster safety bus, and send commands to turn on PDU thruster bus service outputs to TAC A and TAC B.',2,1547,'Step 2',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','CHECKBOX','ORIGINAL',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(7511,'Continue script to fire thruster A1 upstream valve and then downstream valve, and verify thruster fire signals with DMM or scope per table below.',3,1547,'Step 3',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','ORIGINAL',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(7512,'Continue script to fire thruster A2 upstream valve and then downstream valve, and verify thruster fire signals with DMM or scope per table below.',4,1547,'Step 4',_binary '\0',_binary '\0',_binary '\0','TABLE','ORIGINAL',NULL,NULL,_binary '\0',_binary '\0'),(7513,'Continue script to fire thruster B1 upstream valve and then downstream valve, and verify thruster fire signals with DMM or scope per table below.',5,1547,'Step 5',_binary '\0',_binary '\0'